WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
Antioch, in the first century.

2
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:05.330
Paul confronts Peter, to his face.

3
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.190
Peter has stopped eating with
Gentile believers, under pressure.

4
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.380
Paul believes the gospel
itself is at stake.

5
00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:15.880
Centuries later, churches
still divide over doctrine,

6
00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:17.520
marriage and the law.

7
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:23.100
Yet in 1965, on the Antrim coast, a new
community began bringing Protestants and

8
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.660
Catholics together.

9
00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:28.230
So does religion divide
people, or bring them together?

10
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.910
In this mission, you'll see how
churches have answered controversy,

11
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.930
from councils to dialogue.

12
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.670
Then you'll map where faith
and secular law clash today,

13
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.900
using five ways of relating
Christ and culture.

14
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:45.150
Your mission: weigh up whether
religion divides or reconciles.
